actor: Claude Code ADOS adoption into existing repository
phase: project_readiness
outcome: in_progress
current_task: ADOPT-EXISTING-REPO
summary: ADOS 1.9.2 capsule integrated into the existing repository. Original root
  files restored, AGENTS.md extended, ADOS paths excluded from Prettier and ESLint,
  PRODUCT_VERSION.md corrected. Final validation pending.
tasks:
- task_id: BOOTSTRAP
  title: Validate the generated capsule before creating its baseline commit.
  status: in_progress
  acceptance: All capsule checks pass and the baseline commit is confirmed before
    product implementation.
  remaining_work: Merge the adoption pull request to establish the baseline commit
    on main.
  evidence: []
- task_id: ADOPT-EXISTING-REPO
  title: Integrate the generated capsule without replacing existing repository files
    or tooling.
  status: in_progress
  acceptance: README.md, CHANGELOG.md and .gitignore keep their original content;
    AGENTS.md keeps its original rules plus an ADOS section; Husky and semantic-release
    remain unchanged; capsule checks pass.
  remaining_work: Run capsule checks and repository lint, then record the validation
    result.
  evidence: []
decisions:
- id: CANONICAL-STATE
  summary: Use the declared canonical state files and immutable checkpoint history
    for project continuity.
  reason: A single active checkpoint prevents independent state copies from silently
    diverging during agent replacement.
  evidence:
  - docs/CONTINUITY_STANDARD.md
- id: PRESERVE-EXISTING-ROOT-FILES
  summary: Restore README.md, CHANGELOG.md and .gitignore to their pre-bootstrap content
    and keep them as untouched legacy files.
  reason: The generator overwrites existing files. CHANGELOG.md is owned by semantic-release
    and README.md/.gitignore describe the live product and its tooling.
  evidence:
  - .agentic-harness/legacy-baseline.yml
- id: EXTEND-AGENTS-MD
  summary: Keep the original AGENTS.md rules and append an ADOS section with hDS front
    matter.
  reason: CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md import AGENTS.md; the engineering guardrail validator
    requires AGENTS.md to reference ENGINEERING_GUARDRAILS.md.
  evidence:
  - AGENTS.md
- id: KEEP-HUSKY-DEFAULT
  summary: Do not chain the ADOS pre-commit gate into Husky; ADOS hooks are opt-in
    via scripts/install-git-hooks.sh, and CI enforces the gate.
  reason: Husky runs in CI through the prepare script; chaining would make semantic-release
    and dependency-update commits depend on Python and checkpoints.
  evidence:
  - AGENTS.md
- id: ISOLATE-CAPSULE-FROM-LINT
  summary: Exclude generated ADOS paths from Prettier via .prettierignore and tooling/
    from ESLint via the lint script.
  reason: Capsule files are hash-bound by checkpoints and coverage records; reformatting
    them would invalidate evidence, and tooling/visual-review contains CommonJS helpers
    that violate the product ESLint rules.
  evidence:
  - .prettierignore
  - package.json
- id: PRODUCT-VERSION-SOURCE
  summary: Product version is package.json managed by semantic-release; maturity is
    production.
  reason: The generated default 0.0.0-prealpha.0 contradicted the released and deployed
    product.
  evidence:
  - PRODUCT_VERSION.md
  - .github/workflows/deploy.yml
blockers: []
no_blockers_reason: No blocker observed; validation is the remaining step for this
  unit.
questions: []
no_questions_reason: The repository owner explicitly requested ADOS adoption and a
  pull request; product scope is unchanged.
validation:
- command:
  - bash
  - scripts/run_all_checks.sh
  status: not_run
  result: Capsule checks will run after this checkpoint is recorded.
next_action: Run bash scripts/run_all_checks.sh and bun run lint, then record the
  validation checkpoint.
resume_checks: Run resume_project.py; compare checkpoint facts with actual Git status
  and files, preserve uncommitted work and rerun applicable checks.
read_next:
- 00-NEXT_AGENT_STARTUP.md
- AGENTS.md
- AGENT_STATE.md
- AGENT_HANDOFF.md
- docs/CONTINUITY_STANDARD.md
checkpoint_id: ados-adoption-integrated
